{
  "release": "v0.1.1",
  "selected_family": "c",
  "selection_rule": "Elite accuracy loss <= 0.01 per type AND (SciFact improves OR GPQA main gains >= 0.03). Neither DAPT candidate qualifies.",
  "caveats": [
    "Single runs; no multi-seed uncertainty estimate.",
    "The c heads use head_lr=0.0003, accum=1, warmup=200 and 2000/3000/3000 steps; dag/da/eb use head_lr=0.001, accum=8, warmup=100 and 3000 steps per type. The comparison does not isolate DAPT causally.",
    "bw1_sr is checkpoint-g20 from a 20-step run, not a fully trained smaller-model control; its context window is 768 versus 2048 for LLaDA.",
    "The g5000 DAPT run warm-started from g2000 with a fresh optimizer; optimizer and RNG state were not restored.",
    "5000 x 16 x 1024 is an upper bound of 81920000 input token slots, not a measured count of unique non-padding tokens.",
    "automation_5pct is retrospective on labeled evaluation examples, not a deployment error guarantee.",
    "These are archived canonical-order reports, not new GPU evaluations. Legacy non-canonical flip figures compared output positions instead of option identities; they are excluded from this summary and the paper. v0.1.1 fixes that metric with regression tests."
  ],
